==== 2. Anomalies ====
Exp A: at 37.23 s i_ref fell from 0.79 A to 0 in ONE sample while the ball hovered at 9.52 mm;
       the ball fell to the stand. i_ref = 0 with the integral at its -0.3 A clamp needs
       e < -(i0 - 0.3)/Kp = -2.98 mm, i.e. a set point above 14.9 mm.
       At 42.38 s the controller re-lifted: first i_ref 0.799 A -> set point ~9.61 mm (integral at -0.3 A).
       => consistent with a mistyped set point (e.g. 0.09 for 0.009), then 0.0095. Not instability.
PASS: Exp A drop: i_ref stayed exactly 0 until the re-lift (controller demanded zero current)

Exp B run 1 (ball turned over): ball rested at 12.132 mm (run 2: 11.924 mm, sweep: 11.904 mm).
  sample-to-sample position jumps up to 0.29 mm (normal hover: 0.021 mm), reading spanned 8.71..12.28 mm,
  last disturbed moment (51-sample std > 0.1 mm) 3.49 s after switch-on. The controller never lost the ball.
  after the turn, hover current at 11 / 10 mm: run 1 0.975 / 0.902 A, run 2 0.971 / 0.897 A
  slow swing while turning over: 2.3 Hz; Exp A 11.5 mm wobble: 2.4 Hz; 1-D model modes: >= 6 Hz
  -> both at a similar ~2.5 Hz that the vertical model (nominal sensor gain) lacks; cause open
     (2026-11-16: the 11.5 mm wobble is tied to the stand, not shown to be a rotation; see data/lab_2026-11-16/README.md).
PASS: after turning over, run 1 hovers like run 2 (same current within 15 mA): the ball ended in its usual orientation

